Name: pin-init
Source: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/14c897740388216acd59477a382de327d5e27ba4/rust/pin-init
Reference commit: 14c897740388216acd59477a382de327d5e27ba4
Reference subtree: rust/pin-init
Standalone upstream: https://github.com/Rust-for-Linux/pin-init
License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT (original SPDX headers retained)
License texts: standalone upstream LICENSE-APACHE and LICENSE-MIT, retrieved 2026-11-04.
UPSTREAM.sha256 records the original imported files before local modifications.
This is a GN-managed source snapshot, not a crates.io version; gnrt must not regenerate it.

Build configuration
- Runtime: alloc enabled; std, unsafe-pinned, kernel and USE_RUSTC_FEATURES disabled.
- pin_init_internal is a host proc macro. Its syn/quote/proc-macro2 dependencies
  use //external/rust:* declarations and GNRT-generated host recipes. Never refer
  directly to generated vendor paths. Run gnrt sync --all before gn gen.
- This fixed Linux subtree contains no Cargo manifests, so it remains an explicit
  GN source snapshot, like other manually maintained external projects. GNRT
  manages its Cargo dependencies, not the snapshot or its local safety patches.
  Migrating it to a different Cargo/git package requires separate version review.
- Host tests and Miri use the same runtime features as the kernel.
- Examples and upstream documentation are retained for provenance; only the explicitly
  declared contract tests are built here. Upstream documentation may refer to Cargo.

Local source changes
1. Removed Wrapper<T> for MaybeUninit<T>. That wrapper does not drop T before
   invalidating its storage, so it cannot safely accept an arbitrary PinInit<T>.
   A pinned Rust object may register its address and deregister in Drop. Dropping
   Box<MaybeUninit<T>> then leaves a stale registration; the original combination
   reproduced a use-after-free under both Miri models. tests/ui/maybe_uninit.rs
   rejects the combination; contract tests preserve the positive Box/UnsafeCell cases.
2. Clarified cast_pin_init's unsafe preconditions to include pinning/destruction,
   rather than layout/value validity alone. UnsafeCell's Wrapper impl is retained:
   it drops its inner T normally.
3. Marked StackInit, DropGuard and ArrayInitGuard must_use per repository guard policy.
4. Removed trailing whitespace from the imported README and extra final blank
   lines from the license text files; license terms are unchanged.
No initializer/proc-macro algorithm was rewritten. These targeted checks are not
an audit of every upstream API. In particular, the upstream standard Arc adapter
is not BlueOS's planned implicitly pinned Arc.

Checks (board=none)
  ninja -C <out> check_pin_init
  ninja -C <miri-out> check_pin_init_by_miri
Miri requires nightly-2026-05-24 and its MIRI_SYSROOT. Host checks also support
nightly-2024-11-22. The shared Rust compile-test runner checks expected error
codes and a positive fixture using the dependencies of a real GN probe target.
